    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Consider three circles of radius $r$, each of which passes through the centres of the other two circles. The shaded region common to all three circles is called a Reuleaux triangle.\n\nFind the Reuleaux triangle’s",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q15-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"commonBlue\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the intersection common to all three circles\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 39, p39-q15-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{commonBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,{sqrt(3)/2});\n\\coordinate (B) at (-0.5,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (0.5,0);\n\\begin{scope}\n\\clip (A) circle[radius=1];\n\\clip (B) circle[radius=1];\n\\clip (C) circle[radius=1];\n\\fill[commonBlue] (-1.5,-1) rectangle (1.5,2);\n\\end{scope}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A) circle[radius=1];\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (B) circle[radius=1];\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (C) circle[radius=1];\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
