    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "perimeter",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\pi r$.\n\nAdd three arcs, each subtending $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ radians.",
          "worked": "The centres form an equilateral triangle of side $r$, so each boundary arc subtends $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ radians.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=r\\times\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\P&=3\\times\\frac{\\pi r}{3}\\\\P&=\\pi r.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "area",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{r^2}{2}(\\pi-\\sqrt{3})$.\n\nAdd the equilateral triangle’s area and three segment areas.",
          "worked": "The region consists of an equilateral triangle of side $r$ and three segments with central angle $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\triangle}&=\\frac12r^2\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\A_{\\triangle}&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}r^2\\\\A_{\\text{segment}}&=\\frac12r^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}r^2+\\frac32r^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{\\pi r^2}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt3r^2}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{r^2}{2}(\\pi-\\sqrt3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
  },
